w-off, not open to new ideas. Strengths: situational awareness, technical cognition, leadership. Weakness: attitude (show-off, not open) may affect crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as know-it-all, hot temper. Strengths: problem solving, responsibility, concentration. Weakness: hot temper, know-it-all attitude may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. All have some concerns. Which candidate has strongest overall? Perhaps Candidate C has strong situational awareness and leadership, but attitude concerns. Candidate B has conscientiousness and stress handling but interpersonal issues. Candidate D has responsibility and problem solving but hot temper. Candidate A has decision speed and calm but poor communication.\n\nWhich is best? Might be Candidate C because technical competence and leadership are crucial, and attitude concerns could be mitigated? But show-off and not open to new ideas could be serious for crew cooperation. Candidate B's nasty remarks are also serious. Candidate D's hot temper also serious. Candidate A's egocentric and poor communication also serious.\n\nWe need to start discussion, maybe propose Candidate C as provisional recommendation, citing strengths and acknowledging concerns, and ask others for more info on cooperation aspects. Provide vote.\n\nLet's do that."}
